--- body ---
## Context

Upstream advanced two releases past the reviewed baseline on 2026-08-31:
`UPSTREAM` declares v1.10.0 (`b132f2d`, reviewed 2026-08-29), upstream `main` is
now v1.12.0 (`b05ed69`), with v1.11.0 (`ee50cea`) between them.
`make upstream-status` reports STALE. The search layer moved +1738/-57 across ten
files, three of them new (`own-words-source.ts`, `vector-salvage.ts`,
`electron.ts`).

## Why this is NOT "re-read all 23 rows"

The first draft of this ticket said re-read the whole standing. Re-scoped
2026-08-31 on evidence, before any of it was done.

- **The page has no consumer.** Every mechanized reference to `spec/README.md` is
  a hygiene guard; `check_progress.py` recomputes the bars *from the rows*, a
  closed loop. There is no CI. The proof is a dangling citation:
  `verification/GPU-CORRECTED-0482.md:189` still cites "`spec/README.md`'s R30
  row" and R30 was retired -- nothing caught it, because nothing reads it.
- **The delivered axis has never moved.** Across the nine times the bar changed,
  `shipped` stayed at 1; every movement was churn in the denominator as the sheet
  went 29 - 30 - 31 - 34 - 23.
- **Nothing is wrong today.** The page is self-scoping ("Measured against upstream
  v1.10.0") and three rows stamp the version into the verdict. Staleness is
  disclosed, not a defect, and `make check` is green: `check_baseline()` fires
  only once `UPSTREAM` is bumped. Not re-baselining costs nothing.
- **Only four rows are worth reading.** R12, R16 and R23 are falsified by what
  upstream built; R10 is the one row where a wrong answer matters (see 0505).

## One correction to this ticket's own first draft

It claimed ten `measured` verdicts rest on `bench/results/smoke-1.10.0/checks.json`.
False. The smoke is five checks; re-running it re-establishes **R10 and R23 only**.
R6's row cites no smoke artifact. The other seven `measured` rows rest on
`0025-x1-recall`, `0264-gpu-arm`, `0482-gpu-corrected` and `0266-cross-lingual`,
which do not depend on upstream's version. And the eight `code` rows are readable
from a plain clone -- they were never author-gated.

## The trigger

Do NOT bump the baseline because upstream shipped; upstream ships weekly. Bump it
when there is a reason to claim currency: the acceptance harness (0032) exists, or
the page faces outward. Until then the four rows below are read as evidence about
v1.12.0 recorded in their tickets, NOT written into the page -- writing a v1.12.0
reading into a page `UPSTREAM` dates to v1.10.0 is what the guard exists to refuse.

## Exit criteria
- [x] R10 re-read against v1.12.0 -- does #39's silent local-API-to-Web-API fallback touch "MUST NOT leave this machine"? (shared with 0505) -- it does not reach a running build, which pins its API and fails rather than re-routing; `verification/UPSTREAM-1.12.0-REREAD.md`, and logged on 0505
- [x] R12, R16, R23 re-read against v1.12.0 from a clone; findings recorded in their tickets -- the report carries all three, and the tickets those rows cite (0016, 0017, 0022) are closed, so the record lands in the report, in this log, and in `SYNC.md`'s PR #32 row for the one observation that is upstream's rather than ours
- [x] `bench/smoke_upstream.py` repaired before any re-run (see 0506: check 2 asserts retired R28) -- honoured by not re-running. The repair is 0506's and now blocks 0520, because an unrepaired smoke at a new baseline demotes R10 and R23 from `measured` to `code`
- [x] A decision recorded on WHEN to bump: the trigger above, or a different one -- three triggers, any one sufficient, proposed in `spec/DECISIONS.md`'s awaiting list. The third is new evidence from this read: the page under-reports what upstream delivered rather than being merely dated
- [ ] If and when bumped: `UPSTREAM` names v1.12.0 / `b05ed69a88e3a0c1ef874f57f97a0e11ddf7ec3c`; every one of the 24 rows re-read; `make check` and `make upstream-status` green together -- NOT TRIGGERED, and moved to ticket 0520, which exists so `SYNC.md`'s pointer has a live address once this ticket closes
